pre-push guards the public repo (origin, github.com/hanzoai/cloud).
It refuses a push to origin when either is true:
  HISTORY  a pushed commit is reachable from a non-origin remote's ref.
           Refs you never fetched are not consulted, so a fresh clone still
           pushes.
  IMPORTS  a pushed .go or go.mod blob references github.com/hanzo-inc/...
           or hanzoai/licensing. It reads the commits' trees, not your working
           tree.
The hook runs git, grep and awk only. Other remotes and branch deletions are
not checked.  Install:  git config core.hooksPath .githooks
